🧬 ASO–Exosome Computational Study

This repository contains the in silico workflow, input files, and analysis scripts for our study on antisense oligonucleotide (ASO)–loaded exosomes targeting ELF3 and MED23 in osteoarthritic chondrocytes.

We used our tailor-made platform CGMedica, integrated with GROMACS, CHARMM-GUI, and external tools for membrane/exosome modeling, permeation, docking, and retention analysis.

🔑 Key Features

ASO design: ELF3 and MED23 antisense oligos with LNA (+) and PS (*) modifications

Membrane modeling: Healthy vs. osteoarthritic chondrocyte membranes with altered lipid compositions

Exosome engineering: Peptide-modified exosomes (TRPV4, Piezo-based ligands) for selective targeting

Molecular simulations: Constant-pH MD at pH 6.6 (OA) and pH 7.4 (healthy), CHARMM36-july2023 force field

Analysis: Permeation nanosecond timescales, ASO retention %, peptide conformational changes

Decision-tree workflow: Built-in fallback strategies for unstable simulations or poor retention

